# TestClientCode - Source of Truth Rules

> **Purpose**: Rules for working with TestClientCode projects (JS/TS client-side code).

---

## 5 Core Sources of Truth (CRITICAL)

Before making ANY changes to core logic, type definitions, or runtime behavior, you **MUST** read and verify against these files:

| # | Type | Source File |
|---|------|-------------|
| 1 | JS Runtime | `DynamicsCrm.DevKit.Shared\Resources\js\devkit.js` |
| 2 | JS Definitions | `DynamicsCrm.DevKit.Shared\Resources\js\devkit.d.ts` |
| 3 | TS Runtime | `DynamicsCrm.DevKit.Shared\Resources\ts\devkit.ts` |
| 4 | TS Definitions | `DynamicsCrm.DevKit.Shared\Resources\ts\devkit.d.ts` |
| 5 | TS Build | `DynamicsCrm.DevKit.Shared\Resources\ts\build.js` |

> [!CAUTION]
> Do not edit these files without explicit instruction and assessing the impact on the entire toolkit.

